meta {
  name: Access groups - Add a member
  type: http
  seq: 79
}

post {
  url: {{BASE_URL}}/api/v1/communities/nswswk8w8wso0ko8owwk8k0w/access-groups/<group cuid>/members
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "email": "ada@example.com"
  }
}

docs {
  Adds a member of the community to the group (#1241), named by exactly one of member (user cuid), username or email. Adding a member twice changes nothing, so a sync from another system can send its list again. Someone who is not a member of the community gives a validation issue. Owner, admins, moderators with the manage members right. Token ability: groups:write.
}
